---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Mastery Tutor Support"
  description="Support and troubleshooting for Mastery Tutor."
  lang="en"
>
  <article class="page">
    <h1>Mastery Tutor Support</h1>

    <h2>Source and issues</h2>
    <p>
      Source code, release notes, and issue tracking are available at
      <a href="https://github.com/oozoofrog/mastery-tutor">github.com/oozoofrog/mastery-tutor</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      For bugs, privacy questions, or compatibility problems, open a
      <a href="https://github.com/oozoofrog/mastery-tutor/issues/new">GitHub issue</a> with the smallest reproducible example you can provide.
    </p>

    <h2>App wrapper</h2>
    <p>
      The v0.8.0 app wrapper is a stateless Cloudflare Worker exposing a read-only MCP tool named
      <code>tutor_state</code>. It does not require a user account or OAuth.
    </p>

    <h2>Before reporting a problem</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Confirm the Skill or plugin version.</li>
      <li>For MCP issues, verify the remote endpoint responds at <code>/health</code>.</li>
      <li>Use MCP Inspector to confirm <code>tutor_state</code> is listed and callable.</li>
      <li>Include the ChatGPT plan and surface because app and plugin availability can vary.</li>
      <li>Do not include passwords, tokens, private account identifiers, or unrelated sensitive data.</li>
    </ul>

    <nav class="links">
      <a href="/mastery-tutor/">Mastery Tutor</a>
      <a href="/mastery-tutor/privacy/">Privacy</a>
      <a href="/mastery-tutor/terms/">Terms</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto 4rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  h1, h2 { color: var(--dark-green); }
  h2 { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 3rem; }
</style>
